==Norman==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nrf|fro|tirer||to draw, pull out with great effort, snatch violently, tear away}}, of uncertain origin; possibly from {{der|nrf|got|*𐍄𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear away, remove}}, from {{der|nrf|gem-pro|*teraną||to tear, tear apart}}, from {{der|nrf|ine-pro|*derə-||to tear, tear apart}}. If derived from the Germanic word, cognate with {{cog|got|𐌳𐌹𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear apart}}, {{m|got|𐌲𐌰𐍄𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear down, remove}}, {{cog|de|zerren||to tug}}. Alternatively from a reduction of Old French {{m|fro|martirier}}, from {{inh|nrf|LL.|*martyrāre}}.

===Verb===
{{nrf-verb|ger=tith'thie}}

# {{lb|nrf|Jersey}} to [[pull]]
# {{lb|nrf|Jersey}} to [[shoot]]

